hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3043","**\nNarrated to us Ali ibn Hujr, narrated to us Isma'il ibn Ja'far, narrated to us 'Amr—he is Ibn Abi 'Amr—on the authority of 'Abdur-Rahman al-A'raj, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) encountered an elderly man being led between his two sons, leaning upon them. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n\What is the matter with this elderly man?\""\n\nHis two sons replied: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" he took a vow to perform Hajj on foot.\""\n\nSo the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Ride"","" O elderly man"","" for indeed Allah is free from your need and from your vow.\""\n\n---"""""
"3044","**\nNarrated to us Al-Sana'ani; narrated to us Bisr; narrated to us Humaid, who said: I either heard from Anas or it was narrated to us from Thabit, from Anas.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad; narrated to us Abd al-Samad; narrated to us Humaid, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw an elderly man being supported between his two sons. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked, \What is this?\"" They said"","" \""He vowed to walk to the House (the Ka'bah).\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""Indeed"","" Allah is in no need of this man torturing himself.\"" Then he (ﷺ) commanded him to ride."""""
